>> Actually, the words "rustproof", "erodeproof", "corrodeproof", and 
>> "fireproof" all mean the same thing when you wish.  When you specify any of
>> them, nethack records that the item is erodeproof.  Then when you do an 
>> inventory (if they are identified), then you see them as the appropriate 
>> kind of erodeproof.
>
>Interesting.  What items (if any) appear in your inventory as
>"corrodeproof" or "erodeproof"?  I've only seen "fireproof" and
>"rustproof".

Nothing ever appears as "erodeproof", but you can use it when wishing.
Only copper (and bronze) things appear as corrodeproof.  (Think of
erodeproof as being an abstract class).  I think the only thing really
affected by this is bronze plate mail.  (Other copper things like tools
and rings don't corrode).

